]. Glycosylation reduces the aggregation propensity of FUS, with mucin‐type O‐glycosylation regulating its phase separation [
166
]. Impaired FUS glycosylation leads to abnormal SG solidification, disrupted RNA metabolism, and motor neuron death [
165
,
